---
// src/pages/why.astro — SEO page: the benefits of rooting. Keyword target:
// "why root android" / "benefits of rooting android" (and the "is rooting
// worth it" long tail). CONTENT page: zero JavaScript (AGENTS.md rule 4);
// the sitewide OG card stays. Hero art reuses /img/why-root.webp (the SU
// firewall-shield illustration, also on the landing "Why root?" section).
// Benefit claims are restricted to what this repo already publishes:
//   - src/content/guides/what-is-rooting.md — full backups, bloatware
//     removal, hosts-level ad/tracker blocking, custom ROMs (newer Android
//     on abandoned phones), firewall/permission control, Play Integrity
//     cat-and-mouse for banking apps.
//   - src/pages/index.astro "Why root?" — per-app firewall, system-wide ad
//     blocker; Guardian Angel FREE tier has a DNS-based ad blocker (the
//     no-root partial alternative cited in the FAQ).
//   - src/pages/LineageOS.astro — LineageOS keeps devices on a current
//     Android version after the maker stops shipping updates.
//   - src/pages/rooting.astro — deep customization (theming, kernels,
//     automation), unlock factory-resets the device, warranty risk.
// FAQ entries render visibly in the <details> list below AND feed the
// FAQPage JSON-LD — the two must stay text-identical (structured data
// mirrors copy, same pattern as src/pages/rooting.astro).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What is the main benefit of rooting Android?',
    a: 'Full control over your own device. Root access removes the limits the manufacturer shipped: you can uninstall bloatware instead of disabling it, block ads and trackers system-wide, take complete backups including app data, install a custom ROM, and customize the system far beyond stock settings.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does rooting make a phone faster?',
    a: 'Root access by itself does not change speed — it unlocks the tools that can. Removing pre-installed apps frees storage and background capacity, and custom kernels can tune performance and battery behavior. Results depend on the device, which is why our scanner builds a plan for your exact model first.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is rooting still worth it in 2026?',
    a: 'Yes, when you want what stock Android still refuses to give you: complete backups of apps and their data, system-wide ad and tracker blocking, per-app firewall control, and a newer Android version on phones the manufacturer abandoned. The trade-off is that banking and payment apps check for root via Play Integrity — most can be worked around, but it is an ongoing cat-and-mouse game.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I get any of these benefits without root?',
    a: 'Some, partially. A DNS-based ad blocker — like the one in our free Guardian Angel tier — works without root and covers ads in apps and browsers. Complete app-data backups, bloatware uninstalls, per-app firewall rules, and custom ROMs all genuinely require unlocking and rooting the device.',
  },
]

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
}
---

<Base
  title="Why Root Your Android? The Real Benefits, Honestly Explained"
  description="The benefits of rooting your Android phone or tablet: remove bloatware for good, block ads system-wide, control which apps reach the internet, take complete backups, install a custom ROM, and keep your device on a current Android for years longer."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <section class="hero relative before:pointer-events-none before:absolute before:inset-x-0 before:-top-24 before:h-[32rem] before:bg-[radial-gradient(60%_70%_at_70%_30%,rgba(61,220,132,0.14),transparent_70%)] before:content-['']">
    <div class="container hero-grid relative grid items-center gap-8 min-[720px]:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
      <div>
        <h1>Why root your Android? <span class="hl text-accent">The benefits.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Your phone ships with limits you never agreed to: apps you cannot
          uninstall, ads in everything, backups that skip what matters, and
          updates that end while the hardware is still fine. Root access
          removes those limits — here is exactly what you gain.
        </p>
        <div class="row mt-7">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/scan">Scan your device — free</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/rooting">How rooting works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        <img class="block h-auto w-full rounded-[1.25rem] shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(0,0,0,0.45)]"
          src="/img/why-root.webp"
          alt="Illustration of the green SU superhero Android robot projecting a glowing energy shield that blocks sparks from a brick wall — firewall protection and ad blocking with root access"
          width="880"
          height="880"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pt-10 pb-8">
    <h2>Six benefits of rooting your Android</h2>
    <div class="grid-3 mt-6">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Remove bloatware for good</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Stock Android lets you "disable" pre-installed apps — they stay on
          the device, occupying storage. With root you uninstall them
          properly and get that space back.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Block ads everywhere</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Root enables ad and tracker blocking at the hosts-file level:
          one blocklist covers every app and every browser on the device,
          not just a single browser tab.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Decide what goes online</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          A root firewall puts you in charge of which apps may reach the
          internet, app by app — permission control far beyond anything in
          the stock settings.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Take complete backups</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Stock backups skip app data. Root backups include it — your
          settings, saves, and logins come back exactly as they were.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Install a custom ROM</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Replace the whole operating system with a community build like
          <a href="/LineageOS">LineageOS</a> — a cleaner system, or a
          de-Googled one entirely. Browse our <a href="/roms">ROM
          catalog</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Customize deeply</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          System-wide theming, custom kernels, and automation that stock
          Android refuses to run — features your manufacturer never shipped,
          powered by tools like <a href="/Magisk">Magisk</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <h2>Keep a good phone alive for years longer</h2>
    <p>
      Manufacturers stop shipping updates while the hardware is still
      perfectly usable. A custom ROM like
      <a href="/LineageOS">LineageOS</a> keeps a device on a current Android
      version after its maker has stopped — so rooting is not just about
      more features, it is about not throwing away a working phone. Our
      <a href="/roms">ROMs section</a> lists vetted, device-specific builds
      with their official sources.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <h2>What you can do once you are rooted</h2>
    <p>
      Rooting is the foundation; the tools are the payoff.
      <a href="/Magisk"><strong>Magisk</strong></a> and
      <a href="/KernelSU"><strong>KernelSU</strong></a> manage root access
      itself, and our own <a href="/rootz"><strong>Rootz</strong></a> app
      puts that power to work — profiling, automation, logs, firewall,
      files, and a real terminal on your own device. For the family,
      <a href="/guardian-angel"><strong>Guardian Angel</strong></a> adds
      parental device management with everything encrypted on the device
      before it leaves.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <h2>The honest trade-offs</h2>
    <p>
      Benefits this big come with real consequences, and we would rather you
      hear them from us: unlocking the bootloader factory-resets the device,
      rooting can void your warranty, and banking and payment apps may
      refuse to run. Read the full
      <a href="/terms">rooting &amp; unlocking risk disclosure</a> and our
      <a href="/rooting">rooting guide</a> before you begin — then let the
      free <a href="/scan">scanner</a> confirm what your exact device
      supports.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    {faq.map((f) => (
      <details class="faq-item mt-3 rounded-xl border border-[#2a2f36] px-5 py-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">{f.q}</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 mb-1">{f.a}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
    <p class="mt-8">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/scan">Scan your device — free</a>
    </p>
  </section>

</Base>
